      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen chunked input logprobs processing (`SGLANG_ENABLE_LOGPROB_CHUNK=True`, default chunk size `2048`) runs with an `lm_head` LoRA adapter (`LoRABackendLmHeadMixing._get_lm_head_pass_segments`), `build_lm_head_pass_segments(weight_indices, pruned_lens, logprobs_chunk_size)` in `python/sglang/srt/lora/utils.py` previously:\n1. Materialized a flat per-token Python list `token_wi` of length `sum(pruned_lens)` via `token_wi.extend([wi] * pl)`.\n2. Iterated token-by-token in Python across each chunk pass (`for t in range(start, end):`) to run-length encode consecutive adapter indices.\n\nBecause each request already contributes a contiguous run of `pl` tokens assigned to the same adapter index `wi`, expanding to `O(total_pruned_tokens)` and re-scanning token by token in Python is unnecessary and adds ~20 ms of CPU overhead on long-context prefill batches (e.g., 128K pruned tokens).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Replace the per-token list materialization and inner token-by-token RLE loop in `build_lm_head_pass_segments` with direct sequence-run splitting across `logprobs_chunk_size` pass boundaries in `O(num_seqs + num_passes)` time and `O(1)` auxiliary space (~680x faster on 128K pruned tokens across 8 sequences: `20.6 ms -> 0.03 ms`; ~240x faster across 256 sequences: `19.5 ms -> 0.08 ms`).\n- Validate `logprobs_chunk_size > 0` with a clear `ValueError`.\n- Add unit and randomized differential equivalence tests in `test/registered/unit/lora/test_lm_head_pruning.py`.\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nBuilds on the chunked input logprob and LoRA `lm_head` segmentation work by @hnyls2002 (#31655), @jybsuper (#45892, #34337), @glenliu21 (#46743), and @Qiaolin-Yu (#20071).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Code Formatting guidelines.\n- [x] Add unit tests (`pytest test/registered/unit/lora/test_lm_head_pruning.py`).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41551527792](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41551527792)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41551527870](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41551527870)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41551527794](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41551527794)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
